        "title": "Zoology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Zoology is the study of animals — one of two major eukaryotic kingdoms alongside plants (plus fungi, protists, bacteria). Animals are heterotrophs with ingestive nutrition, typically motile, lacking cell walls, and undergoing sexual reproduction. The ~1.5 million described animal species span ~30 phyla and represent the most morphologically diverse domain of eukaryotic life."
    },
