      },
      "text": "```\nPROTOSTOME vs DEUTEROSTOME\n============================="
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#021",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:zoology:00-overview, git-history:zoology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:zoology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "zoology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "zoology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROTOSTOME (\"mouth first\"):\n  Blastopore -> mouth\n  Spiral, determinate cleavage\n  Schizocoelomate (coelom from solid mesoderm splitting)\n  Groups: Arthropoda, Mollusca, Annelida, Nematoda, Platyhelminthes"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#022",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:zoology:00-overview, git-history:zoology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:zoology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "zoology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "zoology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DEUTEROSTOME (\"mouth second\"):\n  Blastopore -> anus; mouth forms secondarily\n  Radial, indeterminate cleavage\n  Enterocoelous (coelom from gut outpocketings)\n  Groups: Echinodermata, Chordata"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#023",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:zoology:00-overview, git-history:zoology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:zoology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "zoology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "zoology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DEVELOPMENTAL FATE:\n  Protostome determinate cleavage:\n    Each blastomere fate fixed early\n    Remove one cell -> defect (mosaic development)\n  Deuterostome indeterminate cleavage:\n    Fate not fixed at first divisions\n    Separate identical twins are possible\n    Remove one cell at 2-cell stage -> two complete embryos\n    (basis for natural twinning in mammals)\n```"
    },
