        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "zoology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:zoology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "zoology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "zoology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Zoology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TETRAPODA (4-limbed descendants of Sarcopterygii):\n  Amphibia: ~8,500 spp; aquatic larvae; terrestrial adults\n  Reptilia (including birds):\n    Lepidosauria (lizards, snakes, tuatara): ~10,000 spp\n    Archosauria (birds + crocodilians): ~10,600 bird spp + 27 croc spp\n    Testudines (turtles): ~360 spp\n  Mammalia: ~5,600 spp\n    Monotremata (egg-laying): platypus + echidnas (5 spp)\n    Marsupialia (pouched): ~330 spp\n    Placentalia: ~5,200 spp (orders: Rodentia, Chiroptera, Primates...)\n```"
    },
